# Pricing handoff — John Stiles / front-end team

**Default:** Annual. **Reference status:** functional, but not release-ready until the pricing and missing-color decisions below are resolved.

The implementation declares **only existing codebase tokens**. Because those tokens cannot reproduce white-on-blue buttons, pale borders, or the green badge accessibly, it uses explicitly provisional **outline treatments** rather than inventing tokens. Typography weights, layout primitives, and the media-query threshold remain CSS literals where no applicable token exists.

## 1. Single-file reference

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Brightline Forms — Pricing</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary-600: #2F6FED;
      --primary-700: #2459C4;
      --gray-500: #6B7280;
      --gray-600: #4B5563;
      --space-1: 4px;
      --space-2: 8px;
      --space-3: 12px;
      --space-4: 16px;
      --space-5: 20px;
      --space-6: 24px;
      --space-8: 32px;
      --radius-md: 8px;
      --radius-lg: 12px;
      --radius-full: 9999px;
      color-scheme: light;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    /* Browser supplies the light canvas. No new surface/color tokens added. */
    body {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--gray-600);
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: var(--space-4);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    button, input { font: inherit; }

    .pricing {
      max-width: calc(30 * var(--space-8) + 2 * var(--space-4)
                      + 2 * var(--space-6));
      margin-inline: auto;
      padding: var(--space-6);
    }

    h1 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-6); }

    .billing {
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
      min-inline-size: 0;
    }

    .billing legend { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }

    .segments {
      display: inline-flex;
      height: calc(2 * var(--space-5));
      border: calc(var(--space-1) / 4) solid var(--gray-500);
      border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    }

    .segment {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      padding-inline: var(--space-2);
      border-radius: var(--radius-full);
      cursor: pointer;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .sr-only, .segment input {
      position: absolute;
      width: 1px;
      height: 1px;
      padding: 0;
      margin: -1px;
      overflow: hidden;
      clip-path: inset(50%);
      white-space: nowrap;
      border: 0;
    }

    /* Provisional accessible selected state: outline, not solid fill. */
    .segment:has(input:checked) {
      color: var(--primary-600);
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 calc(var(--space-1) / 2)
                  var(--primary-600);
    }

    .segment:hover { color: var(--primary-700); }

    .segment:has(input:focus-visible),
    .cta:focus-visible {
      outline: calc(var(--space-1) / 2) solid var(--primary-700);
      outline-offset: var(--space-1);
    }

    .badge {
      color: var(--gray-600);
      border: calc(var(--space-1) / 4) solid var(--gray-500);
      border-radius: var(--radius-full);
      padding-inline: var(--space-1);
      font-size: var(--space-3);
    }

    .cards {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-4);
      justify-items: center;
    }

    .card {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: calc(10 * var(--space-8));
      padding: var(--space-6);
      border: calc(var(--space-1) / 4) solid var(--gray-500);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .card.recommended {
      border: calc(var(--space-1) / 2) solid var(--primary-600);
    }

    .recommendation {
      min-height: var(--space-5);
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--primary-600);
      font-size: var(--space-3);
      line-height: var(--space-5);
    }

    .recommendation.empty { visibility: hidden; }

    .card h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: var(--space-6);
      line-height: var(--space-8);
    }

    .price {
      margin: 0;
      white-space: nowrap;
      line-height: calc(2 * var(--space-6));
    }

    .amount {
      font-size: calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-2));
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .suffix {
      font-size: var(--space-4);
      color: var(--gray-500);
    }

    .billing-note {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: var(--space-5);
      font-size: calc(var(--space-3) + var(--space-1) / 2);
      line-height: var(--space-5);
    }

    /* Retain the same box in monthly mode. */
    .billing-note.is-hidden { visibility: hidden; }

    .features {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-3);
      font-size: calc(var(--space-3) + var(--space-1) / 2);
      line-height: var(--space-5);
    }

    .features li {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: var(--space-4) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }

    .check {
      width: var(--space-4);
      height: var(--space-4);
      margin-top: calc(var(--space-1) / 2);
      color: var(--primary-600);
      flex: none;
    }

    .cta {
      margin-top: auto;
      width: 100%;
      height: calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-3));
      border: calc(var(--space-1) / 2) solid currentColor;
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      background: none;
      color: var(--primary-600);
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .cta:hover:not(:disabled) {
      color: var(--primary-700);
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .cta:disabled {
      color: var(--gray-500);
      border-style: dashed;
      cursor: wait;
    }

    /* CSS custom properties cannot be used in media-query conditions.
       Exact supplied breakpoint retained; no breakpoint token exists. */
    @media (min-width: 1040px) {
      .cards {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        align-items: stretch;
      }
    }

    @media (forced-colors: active) {
      .segment:has(input:checked) {
        box-shadow: none;
        outline: calc(var(--space-1) / 2) solid currentColor;
        outline-offset: calc(-1 * var(--space-1));
      }
      .segment:has(input:focus-visible) {
        outline-offset: var(--space-1);
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
    <h1 id="pricing-title">Choose your plan</h1>

    <fieldset class="billing">
      <legend>Billing frequency</legend>
      <div class="segments">
        <label class="segment">
          <input type="radio" name="billing" value="monthly">
          <span>Monthly</span>
        </label>
        <label class="segment">
          <input type="radio" name="billing" value="annual" checked>
          <span>Annual</span>
          <span class="badge">Save 20%</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="cards" id="cards"></div>
    <p class="sr-only" id="price-status" role="status" aria-atomic="true"></p>
    <p class="sr-only" id="action-status" role="status" aria-atomic="true"></p>
    <noscript>This reference requires JavaScript to display plans.</noscript>
  </main>

  <script>
    // Source-document values retained. Resolve financial discrepancies
    // before production; do not calculate checkout totals from display prices.
    const plans = [
      {
        id: "starter", name: "Starter", monthly: 0, annual: 0, billed: 0,
        features: ["3 forms", "100 responses/mo"]
      },
      {
        id: "pro", name: "Pro", monthly: 19, annual: 15, billed: 190,
        features: [
          "Unlimited forms", "5,000 responses/mo", "Logic", "File uploads"
        ]
      },
      {
        id: "business", name: "Business", monthly: 49, annual: 39, billed: 468,
        features: [
          "Everything in Pro", "SSO", "Audit log", "50,000 responses/mo"
        ]
      }
    ];

    const cards = document.querySelector("#cards");
    const priceStatus = document.querySelector("#price-status");
    const actionStatus = document.querySelector("#action-status");
    const nodes = new Map();
    let billing = "annual";

    for (const plan of plans) {
      const card = document.createElement("article");
      card.className = `card${plan.id === "pro" ? " recommended" : ""}`;
      card.setAttribute("aria-labelledby", `${plan.id}-title`);

      // All interpolated content is trusted static reference data.
      card.innerHTML = `
        <p class="recommendation ${plan.id === "pro" ? "" : "empty"}"
           ${plan.id === "pro" ? "" : 'aria-hidden="true"'}>
          Most popular
        </p>
        <h2 id="${plan.id}-title">${plan.name}</h2>
        <div>
          <p class="price">
            <span class="amount"></span><span class="suffix">
              <span aria-hidden="true">/mo</span>
              <span class="sr-only"> per month</span>
            </span>
          </p>
          <p class="billing-note"></p>
        </div>
        <ul class="features">
          ${plan.features.map(feature => `
            <li>
              <svg class="check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"
                   focusable="false">
                <path d="M3 8l3 3 7-7" fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/>
              </svg>
              <span>${feature}</span>
            </li>
          `).join("")}
        </ul>
        <button class="cta" type="button"></button>
      `;

      const button = card.querySelector(".cta");
      const label = plan.id === "starter" ? "Start free" : "Start 14-day trial";
      button.textContent = label;
      button.setAttribute("aria-label", `${label} — ${plan.name}`);

      button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
        const requestedBilling = billing;
        button.disabled = true;
        button.setAttribute("aria-busy", "true");
        button.textContent = "Starting…";
        actionStatus.textContent =
          `Starting ${plan.name}, ${requestedBilling} billing.`;

        try {
          // Demo only. Replace with the real enrollment request.
          await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1200));
          actionStatus.textContent =
            `Demo complete for ${plan.name}. No account or charge was created.`;
        } finally {
          button.disabled = false;
          button.removeAttribute("aria-busy");
          button.textContent = label;
        }
      });

      nodes.set(plan.id, card);
    }

    function renderPrices(announce = false) {
      for (const plan of plans) {
        const card = nodes.get(plan.id);
        card.querySelector(".amount").textContent = `$${plan[billing]}`;
        const note = card.querySelector(".billing-note");
        note.textContent = `Billed $${plan.billed} yearly`;
        note.classList.toggle("is-hidden", billing !== "annual");
        note.setAttribute("aria-hidden", String(billing !== "annual"));
      }

      if (announce) {
        priceStatus.textContent =
          `${billing === "annual" ? "Annual" : "Monthly"} billing selected. ` +
          plans.map(plan =>
            `${plan.name}: $${plan[billing]} per month` +
            (billing === "annual" ? `, billed $${plan.billed} yearly` : "")
          ).join(". ") + ".";
      }
    }

    const desktop = window.matchMedia("(min-width: 1040px)");

    function arrangeCards() {
      // Reorder DOM, not just CSS: visual, reading and tab order agree.
      const active = document.activeElement;
      const restoreFocus = cards.contains(active);
      const order = desktop.matches
        ? ["starter", "pro", "business"]
        : ["pro", "starter", "business"];

      order.forEach(id => cards.append(nodes.get(id)));
      if (restoreFocus) active.focus({ preventScroll: true });
    }

    document.querySelectorAll('input[name="billing"]').forEach(input => {
      input.addEventListener("change", () => {
        if (!input.checked) return;
        billing = input.value;
        renderPrices(true);
      });
    });

    desktop.addEventListener("change", arrangeCards);
    renderPrices();
    arrangeCards();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

## 2. Developer spec

`calc()` mappings reuse existing spacing tokens; they are not newly declared tokens.

| Element | Property | Value / token mapping | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| Toggle | Height; radius | `2 × --space-5`; `--radius-full` | 40px; pill equivalent to 20px radius at this height |
| Selected option | Color treatment | `--primary-600` | Inspect `#2F6FEB` normalized to `#2F6FED`; **outline replaces fill**, pending white token |
| Selected text | Inspect white | No supplied token | **Changed** to primary text; do not put gray text on blue |
| Unselected text | Color | `--gray-600` | Exact `#4B5563` |
| Annual badge | Text size | `--space-3` | 12px; typography-token alias needed |
| Annual badge | Background/text | No exact tokens | **Changed:** unfilled, `--gray-600` text; replaces `#E8F7EE` / `#1F7A45` |
| Card | Width; padding | `10 × --space-8`; `--space-6` | 320px maximum; 24px |
| Card grid | Gap | `--space-4` | **Changed:** 14 → 16px |
| Card | Radius | `--radius-lg` | 12px |
| Card | Border | `--space-1 / 4`; `--gray-500` | 1px; **changed** from unsupported `#E5E7EB` |
| Pro card | Border; label | `--space-1 / 2`; `--primary-600` | 2px; “Most popular” |
| Price | Size / line height | `--space-8 + --space-2` / `2 × --space-6` | 40/48px |
| Price | Weight | `600`; no supplied token | Semibold; typography-token gap |
| Suffix | Size; color | `--space-4`; `--gray-500` | 16px; exact `#6B7280` |
| CTA | Height; width; radius | `--space-8 + --space-3`; `100%`; `--radius-md` | 44px; full width; 8px |
| CTA | Fill/text | `--primary-600` outline/text | **Changed** from primary fill/white text; missing white token |
| Interactive controls | Hover; focus | `--primary-700`; 2px outline / `--space-1` offset | No geometry changes |
| Loading CTA | Disabled | `--gray-500`, dashed border | Native disabled; label “Starting…” |
| Features | Size / line height | `--space-3 + --space-1 / 2` / `--space-5` | 14/20px |
| Features | Icon; row gap | `--space-4`; `--space-3` | 16px icon; **changed:** 10 → 12px gap |
| Responsive | Breakpoint | `1040px`; no supplied token | Three columns at/above; stacked below, Pro first |
| Billing note | Reserved height | `--space-5` | Hidden—not removed—in monthly mode; prevents toggle-induced shifting |

## 3. Accessibility and QA

- **Semantics:** native radio group inside a named fieldset—not tabs or an on/off switch. Annual’s accessible label includes “Save 20%.”
- **Keyboard:** Tab enters the group at the selected radio; arrow keys change selection; Space selects. Tab proceeds to CTAs. Focus remains on the billing control when prices update.
- **Announcements:** one polite, atomic status announces the selected cadence, all three monthly-equivalent prices, and yearly totals when applicable. Individual prices are not live regions, avoiding duplicate announcements.
- **Order:** breakpoint changes reorder actual card nodes, preserving focused controls. Check reading and tab order at both layouts.
- **Contrast:** on the browser’s light/white canvas, primary-600 is approximately **4.55:1**, primary-700 **6.2:1**, gray-500 **4.83:1**, and gray-600 **7.56:1**. These meet normal-text AA; recheck against the eventual surface token. The proposed white-on-primary treatment is also approximately 4.55:1.
- Test at 320px width, 200% zoom, forced colors, and with keyboard/screen readers. Confirm card bounds stay identical across billing changes and loading states.

## 4. Open decisions

| Owner | Question / inconsistency | Recommended resolution |
|---|---|---|
| PM — **release blocker** | Pro shows $15/mo but bills $190/year; $15 × 12 = $180. | Make annual billed price authoritative; show **$15.83/mo** with a rounded-equivalent disclosure, or approve changing the annual charge to $180. |
| PM — **release blocker** | “Save 20%” is not uniform: Pro’s $190 saves 16.7%; Business’s $468 saves 20.4%. | Replace with **“Save with annual”** unless exact 20% discounts are approved. Exact totals would be $182.40 and $470.40. |
| Designer | Missing white, surface, pale-border and green-badge tokens prevent faithful rendering. | Add approved semantic tokens, then restore filled selection/CTA and intended badge/border colors. Do not ship provisional styles without approval. |
| Designer | Inspect primary differs from code; gaps fall off the spacing scale. | Approve codebase primary and 16px/12px gaps, or formally add required tokens. |
| Designer / engineering | No typography, border-width or breakpoint tokens. | Add dedicated tokens; replace spacing-derived typography and document a shared breakpoint constant. |
| PM / engineering | Enrollment destinations, trial terms, currency and failure behavior are unspecified. | Confirm currency and signup contract; retain the clicked billing cadence through checkout, restore failed buttons, and announce actionable errors. Demo loading is not a real signup flow. |
